<item>
            <title>[LU-20821] conf-sanity test_123aj: cleanup_123aj fails when an OSS has no ost_io device</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20821</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_123aj fails in cleanup, not in the test body:&lt;br/&gt;
  cleanup test 123aj&lt;br/&gt;
  onyx-141vm39: error: executing set_param: No such file or directory&lt;br/&gt;
  test_123aj returned 2&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;cleanup_123aj() in lustre/tests/conf-sanity.sh ends with:&lt;br/&gt;
  do_nodes $(osts_nodes) &quot;$LCTL set_param ${svc}.nrs_policies=fifo&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
with no &apos;|| true&apos;, unlike the two set_param calls immediately above it in the same function. On this cluster (2 OSS, 16 OSTs, 8 per OSS) &apos;ost.OSS.ost_io.nrs_policies&apos; was not available on one of the two OSS nodes at cleanup time, so that do_nodes call returned non-zero; the stack_trap handler propagated that as the test&apos;s own return code, and test_123aj was marked FAIL even though the test body itself completed successfully.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not this patch&apos;s: osts_nodes() and facets_nodes() return the same comma-separated, sorted, unique set of active OST hosts before and after the diff under review (the diff only changes how that string is assembled internally, e.g. moving the comma-join inside facets_nodes(), not its content), and cleanup_123aj() itself is untouched by the diff.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/12b03951-22b4-42bd-bca0-7b0147c3eafc&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/12b03951-22b4-42bd-bca0-7b0147c3eafc&lt;/a&gt; (test_123aj)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-51976-ps6-684d26660414 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/51976&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/51976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
